OL,3,ASetback for SpaceX Starship rocket's
OL,4,Adouble-catch test
OL,5,
OL,6,FSpaceX has aborted its attempt to catch
OL,7,Fthe bottom part of its huge Starship
OL,8,Frocket during its latest test flight.
OL,10,FThe company had aimed to catch it using
OL,11,Fthe mechanical arms - nicknamed
OL,12,Fchopsticks - on the launch tower as it
OL,13,Freturned to Earth, but instead it was
OL,14,Fdiverted to the ocean, bursting into
OL,15,Fflames as it came down.
OL,17,FThe top part of the rocket is now
OL,18,Fcontinuing its journey to space and
OL,19,FSpaceX will decide whether it will try
OL,20,Fto catch this rocket stage at about
OL,21,F15:15 local time (21:15 GMT) on
OL,22,FSaturday.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,317,300,200,140,0,100
